codex
Rejected honestly: no family from this paper cleared G, H, and V simultaneously.

- The paper’s explicit Singer construction requires only 182 modular updates at the largest cap-compliant size; the compact route is equally long, so neither Track A nor Track B applies.
- Compressing that labeling to two recurrence constants gives random-guess success `120/182 ≈ 0.659`.
- A harder theorem-based candidate was broken by a cycle-cover MILP on 7/8 shipping instances. This violates Track A’s G6 requirement. The underlying characterization is Theorem 2.4 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2510.00228).

Artifacts:

- [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2510.00228/REJECTED.md)
- [retained candidate generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2510.00228/rejected_gen_2510_00228.py)
- [attack_audit.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2510.00228/attack_audit.json)
